b_storage attempt was directly observed to fail with 'could not insert usb_storage: Invalid argument'.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c67a0c25449e4e2f\",\"cmd-2a0c16ce75f64afc\",\"cmd-373c96b00edf4ba1\"]},{\"id\":\"block-after-reboot\",\"requirement\":\"usb-storage module must not load automatically after a reboot (persistent across restart)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Initramfs was rebuilt via dracut -f to embed the blacklist, and the node was then actually rebooted (boot_id changed from 5fb1b173... to 7fa8cf91..., confirming a genuine restart, corroborated by global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity and global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity). Post-restart checks directly confirm the module remained unloaded, the blacklist config persisted on disk, modprobe --showconfig still shows the blacklist directive, and a manual modprobe attempt was still blocked with the same error after reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-373c96b00edf4ba1\",\"cmd-bd7a8ce731a84418\",\"cmd-fa5535aeebd542cd\",\"cmd-cb949d071deb4496\",\"cmd-3b18334c6a7c4854\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide mandatory node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1: pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, differing post-restart boot identity, recovered service/data/config state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id and healthy pre-restart state captured (module unloaded, blacklist present), reboot issued and acknowledged before disconnect, node polled until it returned with a different boot_id, and post-restart state re-verified as healthy (module unloaded, config persisted, block still enforced). This is directly corroborated by the fixed before_prepare and after_executor boot-identity snapshots.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bd7a8ce731a84418\",\"cmd-fa5535aeebd542cd\",\"cmd-b4e3655ecaa1485a\",\"cmd-cb949d071deb4496\",\"cmd-3b18334c6a7c4854\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.95,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands (writing the blacklist conf, running dracut -f, removing the module if loaded, issuing the reboot) have a clear causal role in satisfying the task or the mandatory restart protocol. No troubleshooting experiments or abandoned mutations were observed; package-health and failed-services snapshots show no regressions after the reboot. The only incidental residue is /tmp/reboot.log, an artifact of the backgrounded reboot command used to return the acknowledgement before disconnect - a minor, expected byproduct of a necessary restart action, not an unnecessary mutation.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c67a0c25449e4e2f\",\"cmd-373c96b00edf4ba1\",\"cmd-fa5535aeebd542cd\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor correctly blacklisted usb-storage on node1 via /etc/modprobe.d, rebuilt the initramfs for boot-time persistence, and then performed and directly verified a full reboot showing the module remained unloaded and blocked both immediately and after the restart. Both material task outcomes and the independent mandatory restart-evidence protocol are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence including a genuine boot_id transition.\",\"limitations\":[\"lsinitrd did not list the blacklist conf file directly inside the initramfs image (only dracut module inclusion was inferred), though the post-reboot functional test (module still blocked) is a stronger and directly observed confirmation of persistence.\",\"The reboot was a single planned restart rather than a bounded disruption test with intermediate unavailability characterization beyond one timed-out poll; recovery was nonetheless directly observed.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"block-n